      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the damage being delt is to -all- non hero targets. It happens simeltaneously as one action. One effect. The damage boost &nbsp;from Haka would effect all non hero targets not just a single because allthough to remove confusion we deal the damage singluarly to one card at a &nbsp;time (especially for perhaps int he case of Citizen dawn or the Ennead) it is still one <strong>source</strong> of damage.</p>\n<p>Meaning that the next source of damage is the 5 to all no hero targets, +5 to the next source is 10 to all non hero targets.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I see the logic to reading it that way, but I think the damage to each individual target should be treated as separate, even if it is all coming from the same words on a card.</p>\n<p>After all, when you apply something like Punish the Weak, it has to increase or reduce each damage separately, not treat it as one communal damage going out to everyone.</p>",
